-F-YvyVOK0k5QD7lrLOg","name":"Muriel's Jackson Square","shared_categories":"Cajun/Creole, Restaurants","shared_category_count":2},{"business_id":"JhpRI9m71ybWHkAqRdL0Tg","name":"The Avenue Pub","shared_categories":"Restaurants, Southern","shared_category_count":2},{"business_id":"kdqoDMuvyNedsouc1i33vQ","name":"Araña Taqueria y Cantina","shared_categories":"Restaurants","shared_category_count":1},{"business_id":"_Bi9kN_eR75G1eqIl7S3pA","name":"The Bulldog","shared_categories":"Restaurants","shared_category_count":1},{"business_id":"AU-B663F3MPO7W-goWwwXA","name":"B Mac's","shared_categories":"","shared_category_count":0},{"business_id":"pKykk7lnD6Tf9wSzJYRyJA","name":"Starbucks","shared_categories":"","shared_category_count":0}],"text":[{"business_id":"HKdAOvtDv47zPjceCjbz4Q","review_id":"kqiNsgAJvsErszW7drw1TQ","date":"2012-08-07T06:25:35","stars":4,"text_representativeness":0.9465922117233276,"text_excerpt":"This was exactly the sort of place I was pining for when I came to New Orleans with my girlfriend. Yum. We'd had a drink at a bar on Bourbon Street already, and headed down here to get dinner at the recommendation of our hotel's concierge. The recommendation was great, and the hotel gave us a coupon for a free appetizer. For a California boy who has looked at New Orleans creole and cajun food from afar with curiosity for so long, this place was a total hit. The two of us got drinks, and I have to love the irony of a signature Bourbon Street drink being called the Hurricane. Not what I'd normally order to drink, but it was sweet and delicious in context. We had crawfish cakes and oysters t..."},{"business_id":"HKdAOvtDv47zPjceCjbz4Q","review_id":"nSuAGBamk4gOT_x5gNmzzQ","date":"2011-12-02T15:17:24","stars":4,"text_representativeness":0.9452129006385803,"text_excerpt":"So here Niki and I are on Bourbon Street in The Big Easy. It's our first day and her first time here and we are both hungry. Now one would believe that you couldn't find good eats on a street known for Strip Clubs, Theme Bars, Sex shops but that is simply not the case in New Orleans. While walking up and down I noticed a place called La Bayou. The menu looked great and the prices were very reasonable so we gave it a try. The atmosphere here is straight up Gator Alley which easily explains the name of the place. Fancy??? Not at all but we were seated right away and our drink order taken promptly. I do like good service. After scanning the menu I decided to start with raw oysters and for th..."},{"business_id":"HKdAOvtDv47zPjceCjbz4Q","review_id":"onhHyVLwgUZ3jKRFfqH9zw","date":"2014-07-22T21:12:36","stars":5,"text_representativeness":0.9379265308380127,"text_excerpt":"Directly on Bourbon St., in the heart of the action. We came here with 8 STARVING GIRLS! We certainly were not here for any games. Day drinking. Means food soon there after. We came here based off the recommendation of one of the girls who married a local. (and because Acme Oyster House had a dumb long line that no one wants to stand in. Food loses it's value when I have to wait too long for it. Hahahaaaa!! No lie.) It was a really short line, no longer than 10 minutes. My first encounter was at the bar. I bought 8 Pineapple upside down cake shots!!! THEY WERE DELISSSHHHHHHH!!!!! I found the wait staff to be quite patient and attentive. (But we're 8 girls...with a few beauty queens in the..."}],"visual":[{"business_id":"HKdAOvtDv47zPjceCjbz4Q","photo_id":"dei_AX6ThkJsjaS3tPIX5w","label":"outside","image_url":"/photos/dei_AX6ThkJsjaS3tPIX5w.jpg","visual_representativeness":0.8992208242416382},{"business_id":"HKdAOvtDv47zPjceCjbz4Q","photo_id":"b4a-hveYC93gA9OSz_fQPA","label":"inside","image_url":"/photos/b4a-hveYC93gA9OSz_fQPA.jpg","visual_representativeness":0.8299165964126587},{"business_id":"HKdAOvtDv47zPjceCjbz4Q","photo_id":"csVB0NehHOR2f1LCuT8_OQ","label":"food","image_url":"/photos/csVB0NehHOR2f1LCuT8_OQ.jpg","visual_representativeness":0.8208041191101074},{"business_id":"HKdAOvtDv47zPjceC